---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import Link from "@components/ui/link.astro";
import serverOverview from "../assets/docs/server-overview.webp";
---

<section class="mt-20 md:mt-28" aria-labelledby="panel-heading">
  <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] lg:items-start">
    <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-8">
      <h2
        id="panel-heading"
        class="max-w-xl text-3xl font-medium leading-tight tracking-[-0.03em] text-line md:text-4xl">
        Your lab, from first order to everyday control
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-md text-base leading-relaxed text-cool">
        Order in Client Panel. Manage your server in Cloud Panel. Your service's
        management link takes you to the right place.
      </p>
      <dl class="mt-8 space-y-6 border-t border-grid pt-6">
        <div>
          <dt class="text-lg font-medium text-line">Choose and order</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-cool">
            Client Panel holds plan availability, final prices, invoices, and
            support. Review the selected plan before you order.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-lg font-medium text-line">Open your server</dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-cool">
            Follow the management link from your service to Cloud Panel. Find
            your servers and their assigned resources in one workspace.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="text-lg font-medium text-line">
            See what needs attention
          </dt>
          <dd class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-cool">
            Inspect resource usage, open the console, or review activity.
            Backup, snapshot, and network controls depend on your plan and
            permissions.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <Link href="/docs/getting-started/intro/" style="outline" size="md"
          >See how to get started</Link
        >
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="min-w-0 border border-grid bg-surface p-3 sm:p-4">
      <Image
        src={serverOverview}
        alt="Cloud Panel server overview showing assigned CPU, memory and disk, usage charts, and server controls with example names."
        widths={[390, 768, 1200, 1440]}
        sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 60vw, 100vw"
        class="h-auto w-full border border-grid"
        loading="lazy"
      />
      <figcaption class="px-1 pt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-cool">
        Cloud Panel: server resources and controls at a glance.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
